    {
      "id": "anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices.md",
      "sha256": "e0afb5c187aca1e075f9549153b1e896320bb0539544f66d3293fab4b4b77c92",
      "reason": "The Nino 3.4 index is an anomaly relative to a 1950-2014 monthly climatology, and this fragment fixes that the anomaly is defined only relative to its baseline and that anomalies must not mix seasons (the 12-month seasonal-cycle standard deviations depend on it).",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build each source's Niño 3.4 index as the 5S–5N, 170W–120W mean anomaly against that source's **own** 1950–2014 monthly climatology (each calendar month compared with the mean of that calendar month over the years), not against WOA23 or another source's climatology, which would put mean-state bias into the index.",
        "All four indices share the 1950–2014 baseline (`base_period`), so no cross-baseline offset arises; still state the climatology and the baseline with the result (the tools record both in the result's attrs)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The Nino 3.4 box average must be taken as a surface field averaged over the top level, area-weighted, which is exactly the weighting rule this fragment states for surface means.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The regional Niño 3.4 mean must be area-weighted, Σ T·dA / Σ dA, with the weights restricted to the same valid cells as the data; a plain mean over (y, x) is wrong on a curvilinear grid and on latitude rows of a regular grid."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell.md",
      "sha256": "4acdeba0f49784d4435dbc4eed34ca9777254313daa951641759fa02df24cf64",
      "reason": "The three models' `tos` is upper-boundary top-cell bulk temperature on differing top-cell thicknesses, not a skin temperature, which must be stated when its amplitude is compared with ERSSTv5.",
      "status": "not_applicable",
      "not_applicable_reason": "`tos` is used directly for all three models (no `thetao` substitution, no `depth_level` choice) and the Niño 3.4 region is tropical, so the top-cell-thickness and sea-ice points do not arise."
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "Every standard deviation, seasonal cycle and exceedance statistic here is computed offline from monthly means, and this fragment warns that such variance/extreme diagnostics differ from the online ones.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The monthly climatology removed is the plain mean of each calendar month's values over 1950–2014; day weights do not enter a monthly climatology, and `compute_anomaly_vs_own_climatology` and the index tools build it that way.",
        "The standard deviation of the monthly index measures interannual/inter-month variability only; sub-monthly variance cannot be recovered from monthly means, so do not describe it as such."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "The question assumes \"own native grid with its own published cell areas\", but this fragment records that CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are gn while GFDL-ESM4 output is gr conservatively regridded to 1°×1°, which changes its mask and weighting.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is `grid_label='gr'`: its `tos` is already remapped (conserve_order1) to a 1° grid, so its index is computed on that archive grid with the regridded mask, not on the native tripolar grid.",
        "Resolution differs (CESM2 100 km, MPI 250 km); features narrower than the coarse grid are not comparable in amplitude, a caveat for the model-to-model amplitude comparison."
      ]
    },
